Michael Stieb (mstieb@nyx.cs.du.edu) wrote:
: 	I'm looking for binaries for Nethack3.1 for my XT.  Do they exist?
: Can source code be compiled using Turbo C 1.0 for my XT?

You can find the binaries at linc.cis.upenn.edu:/pub.NH3.1/binaries/PC. The
source is available at prep.ai.mit.edu:/pub/gnu.

As to being able to run the binaries, I run them on a 286-10 and it takes
2-3 seconds per move (at least down to level 10). This will be much slower
on an XT

The source is not really set up to be compiled with any Borland version of
C. The binaries have been compiled with MSC 6.0.

